#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# spoor-profile — drive the first-boot flow from a written business profile
# instead of a live interview.
#
# What it is for: the first-boot interview in AGENTS.md is a conversation, and
# every artifact downstream of it — `.env`, this deployment's conventions doc —
# is written by hand from what that conversation turned up. That is the right
# shape for an owner who wants to be asked. It is the wrong shape twice over:
# for an owner who would rather fill in a file than hold a back-and-forth, and
# for anyone testing this repo's own onboarding flow, where every dry-run
# otherwise costs a human or an agent hand-simulating a set of answers turn by
# turn.
#
# So: a profile file holds the answers, and this script does the mechanical
# half of turning them into artifacts. See docs/non-interactive-onboarding.md
# for when to reach for this rather than the interview, and
# profile.example.toml for the format and what each field means.
#
# Scope, deliberately narrow. The interview exists to capture business
# judgement, and a generator that re-derived that judgement would be inventing
# the very thing the conversation is for:
#
#   - **It only transcribes.** Every value it writes is one the profile
#     already states, or one mechanically derived from several profile values
#     by a rule this file spells out (there are two: `COMMS_ALLOWLIST` and
#     `OWNER_TECH_LEVEL`). It never picks a stack, an autonomy delta, a
#     pipeline stage set or a tracker convention.
#   - **An unanswered judgement question stays visibly unanswered.** Fields
#     the profile format marks `# judgment:` may be left out, and what lands
#     in the conventions doc for a missing one is a `TODO(owner)` line naming
#     what is absent and who has to decide it — never a plausible default.
#     `--explain` lists them.
#   - **It holds no secrets and writes none.** A profile file is a plain
#     document that may well be committed or mailed around; the two secret
#     `.env` fields are always written blank, exactly as STARTUP.md step 4
#     requires of the interview.
#   - **It re-derives no fact it does not own.** The `.env` schema, including
#     which fields are required, is `.env.example`'s — read through
#     `spoor-doctor`'s own parser rather than a second copy of it, so the two
#     can never disagree about what the schema says.
#   - **It touches nothing under skills/ or prompts/, and runs no git.** Those
#     are the judgement half of the flow (STARTUP.md steps 5 and 7); this
#     script reports them as outstanding rather than pretending to them.
#
# Exit status: 0 when every artifact the profile could produce was produced
# (outstanding and deferred items are reported, and are not failures — they
# are the boundary this script is honest about), 1 when the profile is invalid
# or an artifact was refused, 2 when the script could not run at all.

import argparse
import json
import os
